# Counts below are for the full demo dataset (mining.ttl + generated.ttl). The
# generated sites and boreholes contribute additional matches; the named sites are
# the ones placed deliberately to demonstrate the behaviour.
# A LineString where every vertex sits OUTSIDE the query box and only one span crosses
# it. The haul road bends its way across the Pilbara from lon 118.60 to 121.00; the box
# spans lon 119.20 to 120.10, and the span from (118.95 -23.45) to (120.35 -23.35) is
# the only part that enters it.
#
# 9 rows. The one that matters is site-haul-road: no vertex of it lies inside the box, so
# a match can only come from a segment crossing, not from a vertex-in-box test. The
# others are generated points that do sit inside the box.
PREFIX luc: <urn:jena:lucene:index#>
SELECT ?entity ?score WHERE {
  (?hit ?entity ?score) luc:query ("default" "default" "*"
    '{"op":"s_intersects","args":[{"property":"urn:jena:lucene:field#location"},{"bbox":[119.20,-23.60,120.10,-23.20]}]}'
    ""
    20
    0)
}
